OL,3,CDon't light fires in 'tinderbox'
OL,4,CBritain, says Andy Burnham before
OL,5,Cfarms meeting
OL,7,FSmokers who have finished with their
OL,8,Fcigarettes should "take great care",
OL,9,Fhe continued.
OL,11,FAfter the emergency alert was
OL,12,Fdistributed, telling people that they
OL,13,F"should not undertake any activity
OL,14,Fthat could start a fire, including
OL,15,Fdisposable barbecues, firepits, garden
OL,16,Fincinerators or fireworks", Mr Burnham
OL,17,Fwrote on X: "Please do not light any
OL,18,Ffires in gardens, the countryside or
OL,19,Fother open spaces, including parks,
OL,20,Fmoorland and wooded areas.
OL,26,@pD@SOUpD@cO]uD@AOUxD@ZO]yD@MOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/18
